# TheaterShell — the live layout: a stage that takes the space, a chat column
# beside it that does not, no nav rail. Twitch, Kick, YouTube Live and a cam site
# all watch the same way, and this is the one arrangement all four actually use.
#
#     use TheaterShell():
#         use LivePlayer(s)
#         use StreamInfo(s, following, subscribed, openTip)
#         use GoalBar(s.goalLabel, sum(t.cents in Tip where t.stream == s.id), s.goalTarget)
#         box class "x-chatcol":
#             use ChatPanel(s, chatDraft, mod)
#
# Exactly two children, in order — the stage's nodes, then the chat column. That
# is the same convention `layout/split.fct` states for the same reason: a `slot`
# is one hole, not two typed sockets, and the arrangement is enforced by which
# column the CSS grid hands each child rather than by the compiler. `Split`
# documents why a lightweight, unchecked pairing is still the right shape for a
# plain app, and why the checked version is a `wireframe` instead — this is that
# same trade, made for the theater layout in particular.
#
# ── WHY THE CHAT COLUMN IS STICKY AND SCROLLS ON ITS OWN ─────────────────────
#
# A live chat is the one piece of a page that keeps producing new rows for as
# long as the reader stays on it, so it is given its own scrolling region at the
# viewport's full height rather than growing the page underneath the player. The
# stage scrolls with the page — the description, the goal bar, the tip rail all
# want to be reachable by scrolling down — and only the SECOND child gets this
# treatment, which is why the rule below targets `:last-child` rather than the
# container: `layout/vocabulary.fct`'s note on `.fa-use` wrappers applies here
# too, and the wrapper `use` renders around each child is what a positional
# selector actually reaches.
#
# ── THE COLLAPSE IS VIDEO-OVER-CHAT, NOT VIDEO-BESIDE-A-HIDDEN-CHAT ──────────
#
# Below 900px the grid drops to one column and the chat column un-sticks and
# lies down under the stage at a fixed 60vh — shown, not hidden, because a chat a
# viewer cannot reach on a phone is a stream nobody can talk during.
app FacetUI:
    css:
        [data-fa-mount] .x-theater { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) 380px;
                    align-items: start; min-height: 100vh; gap: 0;
                    border: none; background: none; padding: 0; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-theater > .fa-use:first-child { min-width: 0; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-theater > .fa-use:last-child { position: sticky; top: 0;
                    align-self: start; height: 100vh; overflow-y: auto; display: flex;
                    flex-direction: column; min-width: 0;
                    border-left: 1px solid var(--x-line, #2f3336); }
        @media (max-width: 900px) {
            [data-fa-mount] .x-theater { grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr); }
            [data-fa-mount] .x-theater > .fa-use:last-child { position: static;
                        height: 60vh; border-left: none;
                        border-top: 1px solid var(--x-line, #2f3336); }
        }
    component TheaterShell():
        box class "x-theater":
            slot
